A logical property and the physical properties it can map to compete in
the sheet order, whatever the writing mode: `margin-inline-start` is
`margin-left` in a left-to-right horizontal flow, and another side in
other flows. So block and merge edges order them.

`merge(left, inlineStart)` puts `margin-inline-start` last, though `left`'s
rule is defined later. `panel` writes `inset-inline-start: 0` before
`left: 10px`, so `left` comes last, though `anchor` defined the `left`
atom first. `width` is not related to any of them and keeps its position:

  $ refmt --parse re --print ml input.re > input.ml
  $ ../../standalone.exe --impl input.ml -o output.ml
  $ styled-ppx.generate output.ml
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
